      "rev_n_1_6a9818_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_6a9818_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_6a9818",
        "thought_text": "Start by considering the maximum degree of any city in the tree. This could give us an initial estimate for the number of companies needed since each company can handle at most one road per city.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391258.2980978
      },
      "rev_n_2_f0ee7e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_f0ee7e_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_f0ee7e",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy algorithm to assign roads to companies, starting with the highest-degree city and working our way down. Assign roads to companies such that no city ends up with more than one road from the same company, until we either run out of companies or we reach the desired number of 'bad' cities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391258.2981172
      },
      "rev_n_3_409eaf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_409eaf_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_409eaf",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a dynamic programming approach to explore different ways of assigning roads to companies, keeping track of the number of 'bad' cities for each possible assignment. This could help us find the optimal number of companies and assignments.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391258.2981272
      },
      "rev_n_4_f8d0a5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_f8d0a5_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_f8d0a5",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using a greedy approach, consider using a binary search to find the minimum number of companies needed. Start with a range of 1 to n-1 and adjust based on whether the current mid-point value can satisfy the condition of having at most k bad cities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4279269670794730333",
